Q: How can I remove all duplicates from an array of objects? A: <p>A TypeScript function to filter an array to its unique elements, where uniqueness is decided by the given predicate function:</p>
<pre><code>function uniqueByPredicate&lt;T&gt;(arr: T[], predicate: (a: T, b: T) =&gt; boolean): T[] {
  return arr.filter((v1, i, a) =&gt; a.findIndex(v2 =&gt; predicate(v1, v2)) === i);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Without typings:</p>
<pre><code>function uniqueByPredicate(arr, predicate) {
  return l.filter((v1, i, a) =&gt; a.findIndex(v2 =&gt; predicate(v1, v2)) === i);
}
</code></pre>

Q: Proper way to show the docstring of descriptor with Pylance in VSCode A: <p>The problem you're facing <em>(or faced more than 3 years ago)</em> is because <strong>descriptors take the docstring of the variable or function it is decorating, not the descriptor itself.</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>class MyClass:
    @property
    def decorated_function(self) -&gt; float:
        &quot;&quot;&quot;From my decorated!&quot;&quot;&quot;

    assigned_to_variable: float = property()
    &quot;&quot;&quot;From my variable!&quot;&quot;&quot;

MyClass().decorated_function   #&gt; (property) decorated_function: float
                                # From my decorated!
MyClass().assigned_to_variable #&gt; (variable) assigned_to_variable: float
                                # From my variable!
</code></pre>
<p>Custom descriptors work in the same fashion. <em>(answering from python 3.11)</em></p>

Q: How to get base url from RestSharp interceptor? A: <p>It depends on how you configure the client. In the <code>ConfigureRestClient</code> delegate where you would add your interceptors, you would get/set it there when you create the interceptors.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>var client = new RestClient(
    ConfigureRestClient,
    ConfigureDefaultHeaders,
    ConfigureSerialization
);

void ConfigureRestClient(RestClientOptions options)
{
    var baseUrl = options.BaseUrl = new(&quot;https://example.com&quot;); // either set here or in ctor
    var logger = ...;
    options.Interceptors.Add(new RequestLogInterceptor(baseUrl, logger));
}

public class RequestLogInterceptor : Interceptor
{
    private readonly Uri _baseUrl;
    private readonly Func&lt;RequestLog, Task&gt; _logger;

    public RequestLogInterceptor(Uri baseUrl, Func&lt;RequestLog, Task&gt; logger)
    {
        _baseUrl = baseUrl.MustBeNotNull(nameof(baseUrl));
        _logger = logger.MustBeNotNull(nameof(logger));
    }

    public override async ValueTask BeforeDeserialization(RestResponse response, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        await _logger(new RequestLog()
        {
            Method = response.Request.Method.ToString().ToUpperInvariant(),
            Url = _baseUrl + &quot;/&quot; + response.Request.Resource,
            Status = (int)response.StatusCode,
        });
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Otherwise, I don't see any way to safely get a reference to the client from within the interceptor. You could technically store a reference to the <code>RestClientOptions</code>, but a read-only copy is used by the client and if you aren't careful, can get out of sync.</p>
